From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nura rc4j series <rc4j@nura.invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:30:00 +0000
Subject: [RFC PATCH] tu: align userspace VA of BOs >= 64 KiB to 64 KiB

On an A640 (SM8150) the CCU can read the 64 KiB-aligned start of the block
that holds a bound render target; when that block start belongs to another
buffer's unmapped tail the read faults with type=TRANSLATION source=CCU
(freedreno list, 2026-11-09, msg48724).  The kernel recipe aligns
kernel-managed GPU VAs to 64 KiB for exactly this reason
(0073-drm-msm-align-kernel-managed-gpu-va-to-64k.patch), but it cannot reach
a VM_BIND context: there userspace picks the addresses, and Turnip allocates
them from a util_vma_heap with plain page alignment
(tu_allocate_userspace_iova(), tu_knl_drm.cc).  So a Vulkan client keeps the
4 KiB packing that the kernel change removes for GL clients.

Give BOs of 64 KiB or more a 64 KiB alignment in that heap.  Emulating the
kernel change for every BO is not needed for the reported fault, where the
block start that gets read is the one of a render target; keeping page
alignment for sub-64 KiB BOs leaves the heap densely packed.  Client
supplied addresses (VK_EXT_map_memory_placed / replayable BOs) and the
alloc_high direction are untouched; only the allocator's alignment argument
changes.

This is the Mesa side of the experiment, not an upstream proposal: the
measured faults on guacamole come from the GL (gallium) path, which does not
use VM_BIND at all in 26.2.6, so this patch is not needed for them.  It is
here so a Vulkan client can be part of an A/B if one is ever involved.
Completely untested: not built, not run, no hardware.

---
Proposed by the nura rc4j kernel work, not by the freedreno reporters; the
kernel-side original is Gaurav Suman's msg48724 (see the recipe patch 0073).
Reviewed by eye against mesa-26.2.6 and apply-checked, nothing else.

 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm.cc | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm.cc
index 68715b0..5ca246b 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm.cc
@@ -21,6 +21,13 @@ tu_allocate_userspace_iova(struct tu_device *dev,
                            enum tu_bo_alloc_flags flags,
                            uint64_t *iova)
 {
+   /* On a6xx (seen on A640) the CCU can read the 64 KiB-aligned start of the
+    * block that holds a bound render target, so a >= 64 KiB BO has to own that
+    * block start itself.  Smaller BOs keep page alignment, which keeps the
+    * heap densely packed.
+    */
+   const uint64_t alignment = size >= (64 * 1024) ? (64 * 1024) : os_page_size;
+
    *iova = 0;
 
    if (flags & TU_BO_ALLOC_REPLAYABLE) {
@@ -36,11 +43,11 @@ tu_allocate_userspace_iova(struct tu_device *dev,
           * them from the other end of the address space.
           */
          dev->vma.alloc_high = true;
-         *iova = util_vma_heap_alloc(&dev->vma, size, os_page_size);
+         *iova = util_vma_heap_alloc(&dev->vma, size, alignment);
       }
    } else {
       dev->vma.alloc_high = false;
-      *iova = util_vma_heap_alloc(&dev->vma, size, os_page_size);
+      *iova = util_vma_heap_alloc(&dev->vma, size, alignment);
    }
 
    if (!*iova)
